Title: The Tomb Chambers
Order: 18
Production Code: 1x18

EXT. GREAT PYRAMID - NIGHT

AMB: wind over open sand

Two months into the search for Reuel, [[Charlie Vance]] refuses to give up. He and [[Jim Titus]] break into a sealed marble structure they've been digging at for days.

SFX: stone grinding, then silence

A hidden door slides open in the dark ahead of them — and armed figures pour out of it.

Bound, blindfolded, they're carried deep underground and left in a bare marble cell. When the blindfold comes off, [[Ai]] and [[Ababdis]] stand before them.

AI
Why hast thou dared to uncover the mysteries of centuries? Art thou weary of life?

CHARLIE VANCE
(bluffing bravado)
We came for old things, to carry the knowledge home. My people fear little, if there's a dollar and a discovery in it.

AI
(to Jim Titus, gently)
And how is it with my brother? Crisp of hair. Black of skin. How do you treat such as this one, in your country?

Left alone, the two prisoners search the seamless walls for hours before Jim finds a seam in the floor with his knife.

SFX: stone grinding back, a rush of cool air

INT. UNDERGROUND PASSAGE - CONTINUOUS

They descend into a vaulted tunnel network, and stumble on two iron-hinged chests: one of raw jewels, one of gold "hidden by the priests of Osiris."

CHARLIE VANCE
Of one blood, Jim. Whatever else we are, we're that.

They clasp hands over it — and then Jim's foot catches an iron ring set in the floor.

JIM TITUS
I believe it's another box, Mr. Vance.

He pulls. The ring gives way, and a black pit opens beneath them, thick with the smell of musk.

CHARLIE VANCE
The serpents! Jim — fly!

SFX: a rush of movement in the dark, a scream cut short
